Gemma 4 describer weights — not tracked in git (see .gitignore)
=================================================================

The vision pipeline's describer (stage 4) loads the local vision-language model from:

    models/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit/

Expected contents: an MLX model directory (config.json, generation_config.json,
processor_config.json, chat_template.jinja, tokenizer.json, model.safetensors and
model.safetensors.index.json), about 4.8 GB. It runs through MLX / mlx-vlm on Apple
silicon (see requirements.txt).

Upstream source
---------------
Google Gemma 4 E4B, instruction-tuned (google/gemma-4-E4B-it), converted to 4-bit MLX
by mlx-community:

    https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit

LICENCE: the weights are governed by the Gemma Terms of Use
(https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms) and its Prohibited Use Policy — NOT the MIT licence
of this repository's code. They are not redistributable under the repository's licence;
anyone shipping them must pass on Google's terms. The app presents the model to the
operator as "JIC-AnyScan-v1" (see src/Vision/Core.py, CONST_MODEL_NAME, and
src/Vision/Describers.py, CONST_GEMMA_MODEL_DIR).

How to fetch
------------
Using the Hugging Face CLI (pip install -U "huggingface_hub[cli]"):

    huggingface-cli download mlx-community/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit \
        --local-dir models/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit

(models/florence2-large-ft/, the previous describer, is no longer used and can be
deleted.)


FastSAM instance-segmentation weights — not tracked in git
==========================================================

The vision pipeline's stage 2 loads FastSAM-x from:

    models/sam-1/FastSAM-x.pt

Expected contents: the single ~140 MB FastSAM-x.pt checkpoint.

Upstream source
---------------
Ultralytics FastSAM (AGPL-3.0 for the code; the weights are the published
FastSAM-x release):

    https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/fast-sam/

How to fetch
------------
Let ultralytics resolve and download the correct release, then move it into place
(version-robust — no pinned URL to rot):

    python -c "from ultralytics import FastSAM; FastSAM('FastSAM-x.pt')"
    mkdir -p models/sam-1 && mv FastSAM-x.pt models/sam-1/

The pipeline resolves this path from Vision/Segmenter.py the same way the
describer's path is resolved (CONST_SEGMENTER_WEIGHTS); override it per run with
Example/Vision/analyze.py --weights.
